Description: Logitech MX Master 4 haptics and actions ring for Linux
 The MX Master 4's headline features - haptic feedback and the thumb-panel
 "Actions Ring" button - only work with Logi Options+, which has no Linux
 build. mx4ctl talks HID++ 2.0 straight to the mouse over /dev/hidraw and
 brings them back, with no vendor software and no kernel module.
 .
 The thumb button opens an actions ring at the cursor: round buttons on a
 circle, chosen by flicking towards one and clicking. Entries run commands
 or built-in desktop actions, and three of them are dials and toggles -
 scroll over the brightness or volume button to change it (the arc around
 the button shows the level) and click the microphone button to mute it.
 .
 Also included:
 .
  * all 16 hardware haptic waveforms, from the command line or a script
  * haptic intensity and thumb-button force threshold
  * DPI, ratchet/freespin, wheel torque and auto-disengage
  * mouse gestures: hold the gesture button and flick
  * desktop notifications buzz the mouse, with per-application waveforms
  * a haptic tick on workspace changes, and a low-battery buzz
  * mx4ctl timer 25m, which buzzes the mouse when the time is up
  * mx4-wizard, an interactive tuner for the mouse-side settings
 .
 A per-user systemd service runs the daemon in graphical sessions.
